@startuml
title Activity Diagram: 3. Main Branch Workflow (Production Environment)

' This diagram conceptually starts after the "Develop Branch Workflow"
' where code, after successful review, is merged/integrated into Main.

|Git/GitHub|
start
note left: Triggered by push/merge to Main Branch
' Start of "Main Branch Workflow" partition from original diagram
' Manual step: Code from Develop is merged into Main by a developer after review & approval (implicit before this)
:Receives push/merge to Main Branch;
:Triggers Jenkins (Main/Production Pipeline);

|Jenkins (CI/CD Pipeline)|
:Pipeline for Main Branch starts;
:Checkout source code from Main Branch;
note right: This code has passed all prior tests (unit, intra-service, inter-service).

fork
  group Frontend Image Build/Tag (Production)
    :(Re)Build or Re-tag Frontend Docker image for Production;
    |Docker Registry|
    :Push Frontend Docker image (tagged for production);
  end group
fork again
  group Backend Image Build/Tag (Production)
    :(Re)Build or Re-tag Backend Docker image(s) for Production;
    |Docker Registry|
    :Push Backend Docker image(s) (tagged for production);
  end group
end fork

|Jenkins (CI/CD Pipeline)|
:Deploy to Production Kubernetes Environment;
|Kubernetes Cluster \n (Production Environment)|
:Pulls new images;
:Deploys/Updates containers;
:Production application updated;

|Jenkins (CI/CD Pipeline)|
:Notify successful deployment to Production;
' End of "Main Branch Workflow" partition from original diagram

stop
@enduml